  ('furano-japan', '08A', 'Furano', 'Japan', 'Central Hokkaido''s dry-powder secret', 'live', 'verified', 'northernLights', 'Hokkaido', '{"ski","wellness","family","culinary","hiking","ultra","culture","romance"}', '{}', '{"essential","comfort","premier","luxury","ultra"}', null, 'emerging', '{"key_facts":["Geographic centre of Hokkaido (''belly button''); Hokkai Heso Matsuri since 1969 (up to 4,000 dancers, 70,000 spectators, 28-29 Jul)","Furano Ski Resort: 32 km slopes (15 easy/13 int/4 diff), 11 lifts, 245-1,074 m, 829 m vertical","40 courses across Furano Zone (24) + Kitanomine Zone (16); longest run 1,900 m; max gradient 34 deg","Over 8 m (up to 9 m) light dry powder; hosted the Ski & Snowboard World Cup 12 times (most in Japan)","Season ~late Nov-early May (2026/27 28 Nov 2026-6 May 2027); peak day ticket ~JPY 8,000; night skiing both zones","Farm Tomita ~1 million visitors/yr, free admission, 12 flower fields; Lavender East 14 ha (opened 2008)","Lavender blooms late June, peaks mid-late July into early August; Tokachi range backdrop","Tokachidake Onsen = highest hot spring in Hokkaido (active volcano); Furano Winery + Furano Cheese Factory (5 cheeses incl Wine Cheddar)","Ski-in/out beds: Fenix Furano (62 units, Kitanomine) + New Furano Prince Hotel (Furano Zone base + onsen)","~44 km / ~1 hr from Asahikawa Airport; ~128 km / ~2.5-3 hrs from New Chitose Airport"],"safety":{"emergency":"110 police / 119 fire + ambulance (free, 24/7); non-emergency medical #7119; interpreter support on line","hospital":"Local Furano clinics/hospital; serious trauma routes to Asahikawa (~44 km) regional hub (verify nearest ED)","advisory_level":"L1","malaria":"none","yellow_fever":"not required","activity_note":"Winter/ski high-risk: off-piste avalanche (JAN Central-Hokkaido bulletin, nadare.jp; transceiver/shovel/probe + guide), tree-well/deep-snow immersion suffocation, cold/whiteout; Tokachidake is an active volcano (check JMA alert)","fcdo":{"posture":"1","quotes":[],"url":"h